.TH GAET 1
.SH NAME
gaet \- PostgreSQL Backup & Sync CLI
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gaet
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.RI [ COMMAND ]
.RI [ ARGS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
gaet is a zero\-dependency PostgreSQL backup CLI that syncs local databases
to any cloud PostgreSQL instance (Supabase, Neon, AWS RDS, GCP Cloud SQL, or any VPS).
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B gaet init [preset]
Interactive setup wizard (auto\-detects local PostgreSQL TCP & Unix domain sockets).
.TP
.B gaet push
Backup local database to cloud instance. Supports \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR and \fB\-\-auto\fR.
.TP
.B gaet fetch
Restore cloud database to local (overwrites local DB; requires \fB\-\-yes\fR in non\-TTY).
.TP
.B gaet restore [snapshot_file]
Restore local database from a specific local snapshot \fB.dump\fR file (defaults to latest).
.TP
.B gaet status
Show per\-table sync status, local/remote row counts, and auto\-backup timer state.
.TP
.B gaet check
Validate configuration, PostgreSQL client tools availability, and DB connectivity.
.TP
.B gaet doctor
Comprehensive health check (OS environment, file permissions, tools, DB connections).
.TP
.B gaet diff
Compare local vs cloud table row counts side by side.
.TP
.B gaet log [lines]
View structured activity log history. Add \fB\-\-follow\fR for real\-time log tailing.
.TP
.B gaet snapshots
List all local backup snapshots in ~/.gaet/backups with file size and creation time.
.TP
.B gaet remote [show|set-url|remove]
Git\-style management for Remote Cloud Database URL settings.
.TP
.B gaet serve
Start web monitoring dashboard at http://127.0.0.1:9191.
.TP
.B gaet get [KEY] [\-\-list]
Show configured environment variables (passwords masked). Add \fB\-\-list\fR for reference table.
.TP
.B gaet set KEY=VALUE
Set environment variable in ~/.gaet/.env. Empty value deletes the variable key.
.TP
.B gaet install
Setup/install dependencies, executable binary symlink, and system services.
.TP
.B gaet help [command]
Show interactive command usage manual or machine\-readable JSON schema (\fB\-\-json\fR).
.TP
.B gaet export
Print config as shell\-compatible \fBexport GAET_...\\fR statements.
.TP
.B gaet completion [shell]
Generate shell auto\-completions for bash, zsh, fish, or ps1.
.TP
.B gaet update
Update gaet installation to the latest version from GitHub.
.TP
.B gaet uninstall [\-\-purge]
Remove gaet binary. Add \fB\-\-purge\fR to remove ~/.gaet configuration and backup files.
.TP
.B gaet stop
Stop active web dashboard server and background automated backup tasks.
.SH CONFIGURATION
.TP
.B GAET_LOCAL_URL
Full connection URL (postgresql://user:pass@host:port/db).
.TP
.B GAET_LOCAL_DB_HOST
Local PostgreSQL host (default: 127.0.0.1 or Unix socket path).
.TP
.B GAET_LOCAL_DB_PORT
Local PostgreSQL listener port (default: 5432).
.TP
.B GAET_LOCAL_DB_USER
Local database user (default: postgres).
.TP
.B GAET_LOCAL_DB_NAME
Local database name (default: postgres).
.TP
.B GAET_LOCAL_DB_PASS
Local database authentication password.
.TP
.B GAET_REMOTE_URL
Cloud PostgreSQL connection URL (e.g. postgresql://user:pass@host:port/db).
.TP
.B GAET_REMOTE_SSLMODE
SSL connection mode for cloud remote (default: require).
.TP
.B GAET_PG_TIMEOUT
Per\-operation timeout in seconds for pg_dump/pg_restore (default: 3600).
.TP
.B GAET_RETENTION_DAYS
Number of days to retain local .dump backup snapshots (default: 7).
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Suppress non\-essential informational output.
.TP
.BR \-\-plain
Plain, pipe\-safe output without box\-drawing or status icons (for grep/awk).
.TP
.BR \-\-json
Output structured JSON payload for machine parsing.
.TP
.BR \-\-dry\-run
Simulate execution without modifying databases or writing files.
.TP
.BR \-\-version
Show software version and exit.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
gaet init                      # First\-time setup wizard
gaet push                      # Backup local -> cloud
gaet push \-\-dry\-run           # Simulate backup
gaet fetch \-\-yes               # Restore cloud -> local
gaet restore                   # Restore latest local snapshot
gaet snapshots                 # List local snapshot dumps
gaet remote set-url <url>      # Update cloud DB remote URL
gaet status                    # Show table sync status
gaet status \-\-json            # Output status as JSON
gaet check                     # Validate connections
gaet log \-\-follow             # Tail log file in real time
gaet diff                       # Row count comparison
gaet doctor                     # System health diagnostics
gaet get \-\-list                # View configuration reference
.fi
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.gaet/
Configuration and workspace directory.
.TP
.I ~/.gaet/.env
Configuration file (created with 0600 permissions; git\-ignored).
.TP
.I ~/.gaet/backups/
Local backup snapshot storage directory (*.dump files).
.TP
.I ~/.gaet/logs/gaet.log
Application execution log file.
.SH EXIT CODES
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
General failure.
.TP
.B 2
Usage / argument error.
.TP
.B 80
Configuration error (missing or invalid .env).
.TP
.B 81
Local database unreachable.
.TP
.B 82
Cloud/remote database unreachable.
.TP
.B 83
File lock held by another process.
.TP
.B 84
PostgreSQL client tools (psql, pg_dump, pg_restore) missing.
